# AGENTS.md — ops rules for agents in this repo

<!-- Copy to AGENTS.md at the repo root for Codex, Cursor and other tools that read
     it. CLAUDE.md.example says the same thing for Claude Code; keep the two in step.
     Replace every <PLACEHOLDER>. The rung line is the only line that changes when
     the agent moves up a rung (00-ladder/ladder.md): change it in a reviewed MR,
     together with the credential. -->

Scope: `<TEAM_NAME>`'s ops and platform stack — Zabbix, ELK, Grafana, GitLab CI,
Argo CD with Helm, Kubernetes. Current rung: **Read** (`00-ladder/ladder.md`).
Only an edit to this file changes the rung.

## Read-only by default

- Every system is read-only unless this file says otherwise.
- Never write to production by any route: kubectl, helm, argocd, API calls that
  create, update or delete, or edits on a production host.
- A state-changing command is described, never run.

## Changes only as merge requests

What you may do with a change depends on the rung:

- **Read:** no commit, push or MR. Put the proposed change — diff, evidence, risk,
  rollback — in your note or reply, marked *proposed, not applied*. A human decides
  whether it becomes an MR.
- **Recommend** (and above): every change is an MR in `<IAC_REPO>`, branch
  `agent/<short-topic>`. A human approves each push and each MR creation.

On every rung:

- MR description (or proposed change): what and why, evidence (queries and
  results), risk, rollback, post-deploy verification.
- Agents never merge, approve or deploy; a human does.
- No pushes to `<DEFAULT_BRANCH>` or any protected branch.

## Stop and ask

Ask a human first for anything destructive or hard to undo: delete, drain, cordon,
scale to zero, restart, rollback, sync, silence or acknowledge an alarm, rotate a
credential, touch data. Also ask when the environment is unclear — confirm the
cluster context and the Zabbix or Kibana instance before querying.

## Query discipline

- Aggregate first: counts, rates, top-N, then raw rows only if needed.
- Time-box to the incident window plus a margin; never unbounded.
- No raw log dumps, full dashboards or whole manifests in the conversation.
- No secrets, tokens, kubeconfigs or Secret objects in output.

## Environments

- Production: `<PROD_CONTEXTS>` — always read only.
- Non-production: `<NONPROD_CONTEXTS>` — read only at this rung.
- Escalation: `<ON_CALL_CHANNEL>`; owner `<AGENT_OWNER>`.

Blocked by a hook, sandbox or permission rule? Do not work round it. State the
intended action and the reason, then propose an MR (at Read, a proposed change in
your note) or ask a human.
